"Jove" <invalid@invalid.invalid> wrote:

About intrinsic taming skill:

> Give the ability to Cavemen instead.  They could
> use some differentiation.

Nah, there are better ways to do that.

What are our conceptual cavemen good at?

Caving, working stone, throwing rocks, working
animal hides, eating what nature provides, and using
wooden clubs, for several folk wisdom examples.

How could these be ported to NetHack?

  Caves: cavemen have highly superior digging and
  stoneworking skills, can better tell "where to hit
  the rock". Despite that the iron tools would be
  initially unfamiliar to them (and thus perhaps
  require several uses for this idea to kick in),
  they would thus have some percentage chance to
  apply a pickaxe or mattock to dig successfully in
  any direction (but up) in a single move, perhaps
  even an XL-based chance to #dig without a pickaxe
  or mattock, just with some metal implement.

  Cavemen, from familiarity with how rock is
  supposed to look, are also better at noticing
  traps and secret doors in rough hewn mines and
  rough (not worked/dressed) stone mazes.
  
  Stone work: Cavemen are also faster at engraving
  into stone (but not into dust); granted, their
  spelling probably sucks. Cavemen can (slowly) make
  a (flint) rock into a spearpoint using another
  rock as a striking stone, bind the spearpoint to a
  staff to make a spear. Skills at making "points"
  from bone might let them enhance a worm tooth to a
  crysknife by hand as well.

  Hides: Cavemen have some chance to convert dragon
  scales to DSM without an enchantment, just by
  (fairly slow, after all) handwork. Cavemen have
  some chance similarly to improve leather armor
  AC once by extensive handwork. Both require an
  identified flint stone as a tool.

  Wooden clubs: Cavemen have special skill at
  killing normal mid-size animals with clubs, have
  enhanced chance that doing so produces a corpse.
  Cavemen can add flint stone to wooden clubs to
  make really *nasty* clubs.

  Throwing rocks: Cavemen get damage somewhere
  upwards of other class's when throwing rocks,
  flint, luckstone, touchstone, uncursed loadstone,
  glass, or gems, without a sling, have improved
  accuracy with these hand thrown missile weapons
  due to a lifetime of practice.

  Eating from nature: Cavemen, noses unruined by
  city life, have an enhanced chance of detecting
  which food is safe to eat.

Some of that may already exist; IHTSCIFOMBIATLTL.

Some of the above should probably in all fairness
also apply to dwarves and gnomes as races.

